course: dictionary
lesson: 6858
title: Overactive: too much of a good thing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overactive means too active. Something that is overactive works, moves or does more than is normal or healthy. A puppy can be full of energy, but a dog that runs in circles all day and never settles might be called overactive.
explain: The word can also describe a body part or a machine. An overactive thyroid is an organ in the body that works too hard. An overactive imagination is when your mind makes up scary or unlikely things.
explain: Look at the context to find the meaning. «Careful studies found sugar did not make children hyperactive (wildly overactive)» tells you that hyperactive means wildly overactive. The brackets are a clue, and they show that overactive means more active than normal.
fact: Overactive means too active, working or moving more than is normal or healthy.
fact: «An overactive imagination» means imagining scary or unlikely things.
fact: An overactive body part, such as «an overactive bladder» or an overactive thyroid, works too hard.
fact: Machines can be overactive too, when they work harder than they should.
fact: Saying someone has an overactive imagination is often a gentle way of saying they are imagining things.
exercise: «Careful studies found sugar did not make children hyperactive (wildly overactive).» What does overactive mean in this sentence? | Quiet and calm | Very sleepy and slow | * Wildly active, doing much more than normal | Full of sugar
exercise: Mia says her brother has «an overactive imagination» because he thinks there is a monster under the bed. What does this mean? | He draws pictures every day | * He imagines scary or unlikely things | He has a very good memory | He is always tired
exercise: Which of these is a body part that works too hard? | * An overactive bladder | A sleepy kitten | A slow bus | A quiet library
test: Which word means too active? | * Overactive | Gentle | Sleepy | Lazy
test: Which sentence uses overactive correctly? | * The overactive puppy ran in circles and would not stop. | The overactive bread was soft and warm. | The overactive cat slept in the sun all afternoon.
exam: Which word best fits the gap? «Her ___ imagination made the dark garden seem full of ghosts.» | tidy | slow | * overactive | quiet
